error: rsjs boundary: this handler `match` pattern is outside the current Client IR match surface

       Why:
         rsjs lowers handler matches only when the pattern space has a direct JavaScript shape: exact booleans, `Some(value)` / `Some(_)` / `None`, literals, bounded ranges, optional guards, and a final `_` fallback. Path patterns and nested destructuring need richer type-aware pattern lowering.

       Use one of:
         - Rewrite the match to supported boolean, Option, literal, range, guard, and `_` arms.
         - Move path-pattern or destructuring logic into a standalone helper annotated once with `#[rsjs::client]`; reachable calls are linked automatically.
         - Normalize the matched value into a signal-friendly primitive before the handler uses it.

       Tracked feature:
         handler.match
